    <string name="quiz_intro_title">Not sure what to pick?</string>
    <string name="quiz_intro_body">Answer a few quick questions and we\'ll figure out your type — and which genres to start you on.</string>

    <string name="genre_hiphop">Beats and rhymes. The words are doing the work.</string>
    <string name="genre_rock">Guitars, drums, and volume. Loud or moody, take your pick.</string>
    <string name="genre_pop">Big choruses built to stick after one listen.</string>
    <string name="genre_jazz">Improvised on the spot — the same song is never quite the same twice.</string>
    <string name="genre_dance">Made for a floor. Steady kick, no reason to stop moving.</string>
    <string name="genre_country">Someone telling you a story, guitar in hand.</string>
    <string name="genre_rnb">Smooth grooves and voices that carry the whole thing.</string>
    <string name="genre_electronic">Built from synths and machines. Often no vocals at all.</string>
    <string name="genre_kpop">Packed with hooks, switches lanes mid-song, made to be watched too.</string>
    <string name="genre_latin">Percussion you feel before you hear. Reggaetón, salsa, and everything nearby.</string>
    <string name="genre_ccm">Worship songs with pop production — written for a room singing along.</string>
    <string name="genre_alternative">Rock that ducks the mainstream. Not big on following the rules.</string>
    <string name="genre_bass">The low end is the whole point. Best where the speakers can take it.</string>
    <string name="genre_dubstep">Everything builds toward the moment the bass drops.</string>

